# TypeScript incremental build state — regenerated by `tsc -b` on every build.
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vercel CLI link/state for this machine.
.vercel

# NOTE: `public/data/` is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It is generated (`npm run data:generate`) so ignoring it is the intuitive
# call — but `npm run build` never runs the generator, so nothing on Vercel can
# recreate it. Ignored, the deploy ships a `dist/` with no data and every page
# renders empty while the build stays green.
#
# Regenerate it locally and commit the diff. The generator is seeded, so a
# re-run with no code change produces no diff at all.

# Per-machine Claude Code settings.
.claude/settings.local.json
Costing model_ERA_Archive.xlsx

# The ERA workbook — the ingest's second source, 37 MB.
#
# Not committed: it is an order of magnitude larger than anything else here and
# it changes rarely, so carrying every future revision in the history costs far
# more than keeping one copy per machine. `npm run data:ingest` needs it and
# says so by name when it is absent; `public/data/` is committed, so a clone
# that only builds and runs the app never needs the file at all.
ERA dataset_v4 (1).xlsx

# Superseded by the ERA workbook above, which carries the same sheet with the
# latitude column this one lost. Nothing reads it any more; ignored so a stray
# `git add -A` cannot put it back.
Raw data with readiness level.xlsx

# The state coverage workbook — the source of every readiness band on National
# Coverage.
#
# Not committed, for the same reason as the workbooks above: the source stays
# editable outside the repo and the derived data comes in with it. What *is*
# committed is `scripts/source-data/national-coverage.json`, the 37 rows
# `npm run data:coverage` extracts and validates from this file. `data:ingest`
# reads that JSON and never this workbook, so a clone can rebuild
# `public/data/` without holding a copy.
National Coverage.xlsx

# The fetched copy of the assessment sheet (`npm run data:ingest -- --fetch`).
#
# Ignored because it is a byte-identical duplicate of the committed
# `List of gaps and interventions per facility.csv` at the repo root, which is
# the offline source the ingest falls back to. Committing both is 15 MB to say
# the same thing twice. Delete it and re-fetch whenever the sheet moves.
scripts/source-data/assessment.csv
